Neway technician VPN provisioning
===================================

No WireGuard private key or peer configuration is shipped in this image.

A Neway provisioning process must create /etc/wireguard/wg0.conf with:
- a unique device key and unique VPN address assigned in the Neway peer registry;
- only the required Neway VPN peer(s), with a pinned public key and endpoint;
- narrowly scoped AllowedIPs (do not route all machine/customer traffic through the VPN);
- PersistentKeepalive only where required by the network/NAT design.

Set owner root:root and mode 0600. Validate with:
  wg-quick strip /etc/wireguard/wg0.conf >/dev/null

Technician SSH is intentionally gated until the machine serial, TPM device, controller
attestation verification marker, and WireGuard configuration all pass validation.
Never commit real wg0.conf files, private keys, pre-shared keys, or customer VPN details.

Automatic VPN startup
---------------------

After factory provisioning creates the unique wg0.conf, Neway enables wg-quick@wg0.service.
At boot, a systemd pre-start guard checks the factory serial, TPM, verified controller
marker, and root-owned mode-0600 WireGuard configuration before the tunnel is started.
The peer endpoint should use PersistentKeepalive = 25 when the device is behind NAT and
must accept inbound technician traffic only from the assigned VPN address range.

Do not create or copy a shared wg0.conf. Generate one private key per physical machine.
